From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <andrewyoull86@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 17:13:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] RISC OS: speed: draw size, sky background option, RGBA fonts

Pi result of m1-1: 4.8 fps in a 640x480 window. Most of a frame is
filling pixels, so:
- riscosplatform.cpp: on the first run, screen.xml is set to full screen
  at a draw size in the screen's shape, 360 pixels high (576x360 on a
  16:10 screen, 640x360 on 16:9). TORCS's full screen is GLUT's game
  mode, which riscos-mesa's freeglut draws at the requested size and
  stretches over the screen, through a hardware overlay where there is
  one.
- screen.cpp: Display sizes in 16:10 and 16:9 shapes too.
- Graphic Configuration: "Sky background" (graph.xml "sky background",
  default yes). The panorama is a whole screen of textured pixels drawn
  before the scene every frame (18% of a host profile frame); without it
  the sky is the track's background colour.
- guifont.cpp: font textures RGBA in GL_CLAMP_TO_EDGE on software OpenGL
  (luminance-alpha in GL_CLAMP took Mesa's general path).
- riscosplatform.cpp: the settings files are replaced when the
  application's version (its Version file) differs from the one recorded
  in the settings (riscos-version), instead of when the application's copy
  is newer: a Pi without a working clock can start with a date earlier
  than the zip's files, and the settings saved in the game then looked
  older and were replaced at every start (Pi test of m2-1: switching to
  window mode didn't stick).
